Thanks, we'll investigate this issue.
@xxshady please be aware that when rust is compiled to WASM, you can't have unwinding panics; every panic is an abort. The fix to this problem would be to abort the entire WASIX process when a thread panics, which is also the native behavior with `panic = 'abort'`. This may not be what you expected the fix to be.

Interestingly, my testing shows that calling `exit()` from a non-main thread is also broken, with the same underlying reason as this issue.

