problem_statement:
OTEL root context is undefined by default
Version: Deno 2.2.1

Trying to run simple code using OTEL api:
```ts
import { trace } from 'npm:@opentelemetry/api@1';

const a = trace.getTracer('foo');

a.startActiveSpan('bar', span => {
	span.addEvent('baz');
	span.end();
});
```

```shell
$ deno run --unstable-otel -A demo.ts 
error: Uncaught (in promise) TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'setValue')
a.startActiveSpan('bar', span => {
  ^
    at Tracer.startActiveSpan (ext:deno_telemetry/telemetry.ts:76:39)
    at file:///path/to/demo.ts:5:3
```

Because there is no active root context at this point

Only when entered manually:
```ts
import { trace, context } from 'npm:@opentelemetry/api@1';

const root = context.active();
const a = trace.getTracer('foo');

context.with(root, () => {
	a.startActiveSpan('bar', span => {
		span.addEvent('baz');
		span.end();
	});
});
```
This code runs successfully.

