This is my current workaround but I don't see a reason why the parameter shouldn't still be available:
```js
const maxIterations = 30;
let n = 0;

Deno.bench("n iterations", () => {
    if (n < maxIterations) {        
        console.log('Completed:', n);
    }

    n += 1;
});
```

