problem_statement:
feature: arri generators should be able to generate objects that have no properties
a schema like this

```typescript
const EmptyObject = a.object({});
```

Will cause arri generators to output invalid code. Adding support for empty objects is useful because it makes it easier to have a fallback value in the case of discriminator schemas.

```typescript
const Shape = a.discriminator("Shape", {
  UNKNOWN: a.object({}), // fallback value
  RECT: a.object({
    width: a.float64(),
    height: a.float64(),
  }),
  CIRCLE: a.object({
    radius: a.float64(),
  }),
});

```

Without this we have to add some dummy field to the `UNKNOWN` option which isn't great.

